Z||000000||Brian84SE||02-21-2000||09:09 PM||||OK, here's a simple question. Haynes says each notch on the timing scale is 2 degrees. (and I can barely make out lines in between each notch) but I couldnt see how many degrees the scale actually represents and Haynes says nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||02-21-2000||09:16 PM||||I never could read those marks so I just bought a "dial back to zero" timing light. If you have never used one, they are great. It has a degreed knob on the back of it. You just aim, shoot and dial the knob until the timing mark lines up at 0 degrees. Then look at the knob and it shows how much timing you have. Comes in great when trying to set vacuum and mechanical advance limits on older cars.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian84SE||02-21-2000||09:46 PM||||It's a 4cyl.||||reg||1
